    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d181">

                <pb facs="0550" n="500" xml:id="pg500"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Paris Peace Conf. 184.011/51c: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Commission to Negotiate
                            Peace to the Minister in Switzerland</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Stovall</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Paris</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-01-30T22:00:00+00:00">January 30, 1919—10
                        p.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>67. For Coolidge. “Your dispatches No. 31 January 20th and 33 January 22d.<anchor
                        n="47" xml:id="d181-f1"/> Attempts to settle boundary disputes by American
                    representatives should in future be avoided as outside of scope your mission.
                    Such action even if temporary can only properly be taken by Interallied
                    representatives and an assumption by United States of office of sole arbiter may
                    well prove embarrassing. In this case Commission neither ratifies nor disavows
                    action taken but will not unless occasion requires interfere with <hi
                        rendition="#italic">statu quo.</hi></p>
                <closer><hi rendition="#small-caps">Am</hi>[<hi rendition="#small-caps">erican</hi>]
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Mission</hi></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
